    {
      "id": "g_topic_particle",
      "grammar": true,
      "english": "I am a student. (저는 … 이에요/예요)",
      "word": "저는 학생이에요",
      "romanized": "jeoneun haksaeng-ieyo",
      "grammarNote": "**은/는** marks the topic (**는** after a vowel, **은** after a consonant). **이에요/예요** = polite 'is/am/are' (**이에요** after a consonant, **예요** after a vowel):\n**저는 학생이에요** (I'm a student). **저** = I (humble).",
      "englishPhrase": "I'm Korean.",
      "phrase": "저는 한국 사람이에요.",
      "phraseRomanized": "Jeoneun hanguk saram-ieyo.",
      "literal": [
        [
          "저는",
          "I-(topic)"
        ],
        [
          "한국 사람",
          "Korean"
        ],
        [
          "이에요",
          "am"
        ]
      ],
      "format": "table",
      "table": {
        "title": "Particles change with the final sound",
        "rows": [
          [
            "topic",
            "은 (after consonant) / 는 (after vowel)"
          ],
          [
            "subject",
            "이 / 가"
          ],
          [
            "object",
            "을 / 를"
          ]
        ],
        "note": "학생은, 저는 · 눈이, 커피가 · 밥을, 커피를"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g_object_sov",
      "grammar": true,
      "english": "I eat rice. (object 을/를, verb last)",
      "word": "밥을 먹어요",
      "romanized": "bab-eul meogeoyo",
      "grammarNote": "Korean is **Subject–Object–Verb** — the verb comes last. **을/를** marks the object (**을** after a consonant, **를** after a vowel):\n**밥을 먹어요** (eat rice), **물을 마셔요** (drink water).",
      "englishPhrase": "I drink coffee.",
      "phrase": "커피를 마셔요.",
      "phraseRomanized": "Keopireul masyeoyo.",
      "literal": [
        [
          "커피",
          "coffee"
        ],
        [
          "를",
          "(obj)"
        ],
        [
          "마셔요",
          "drink"
        ]
      ],
      "format": "cloze",
      "cloze": {
        "prompt": "I eat rice. (object particle)",
        "text": "밥___ 먹어요",
        "answer": "을 (eul)",
        "options": [
          "을",
          "를"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g_yo_politeness",
      "grammar": true,
      "english": "to eat → eats (polite -요 ending)",
      "word": "먹어요",
      "romanized": "meogeoyo",
      "grammarNote": "The **-요** ending makes speech polite but friendly — the everyday standard:\n**먹어요** (eat), **가요** (go), **마셔요** (drink). Drop **요** for casual speech with close friends: **먹어**. **-ㅂ니다/습니다** is the formal ending.",
      "englishPhrase": "I go to school.",
      "phrase": "학교에 가요.",
      "phraseRomanized": "Hakgyoe gayo.",
      "literal": [
        [
          "학교",
          "school"
        ],
        [
          "에",
          "to"
        ],
        [
          "가요",
          "go"
        ]
      ],
      "format": "produce",
      "produce": {
        "concept": "Polite speech ends in -요",
        "task": "say: (I) eat",
        "answer": "먹어요 meogeoyo",
        "gloss": "Add -아/어요 to the verb stem; dropped in casual speech."
      }
    },
    {
