      "english": "Are you a student? (same form, rising tone)",
      "word": "학생이에요?",
      "romanized": "haksaeng-ieyo?",
      "grammarNote": "In polite **-요** speech, a yes/no question looks **identical to the statement** — only the rising intonation (and the '?') changes:\n**학생이에요.** (You're a student.) → **학생이에요?** (Are you a student?). Nothing is added or reordered.",
      "englishPhrase": "Are you okay?",
      "phrase": "괜찮아요?",
      "phraseRomanized": "Gwaenchanayo?",
      "literal": [
        [
          "괜찮아요",
          "okay"
        ],
        [
          "?",
          "[?]"
        ]
      ],
      "format": "contrast",
      "contrast": {
        "prompt": "Statement vs yes/no question (same words)",
        "a": {
          "term": "학생이에요. haksaeng-ieyo.",
          "gloss": "statement — falling tone"
        },
        "b": {
          "term": "학생이에요? haksaeng-ieyo?",
          "gloss": "question — rising tone only"
        }
      }
    },
